  "title": "Mexico City",
  "summary": "Mexico City was built in the 16th century on the ruins of Tenochtitlan, the Mexica capital on an island in Lake Texcoco, after the Spanish destroyed the city and drained the lake. It became the capital of New Spain, with a grid plan. The Templo Mayor was built over and has been excavated systematically since the late 1970s in the downtown. Its historic centre was listed by UNESCO in 1987.",
